    "summary": "docs-review-client.ts: decide(mdPath, decision, comments) calls 'workflow.reviewDecision' once with the path as given (the id map is not consulted) and throws on the { error } arm; approve() and comment() are removed; content() forwards docPath, contentVersion, feedback, reviewer and state, each an absent key when the daemon sent none. protocol.ts: 'docs-decision' is { artifactId, decision, comments }; 'docs-decision-result' and 'docs-companion' are host messages and 'open-companion' is a webview message, each in its kind list. Because the client's methods and the message shape changed, the pane's host (docs-review-panel.ts, a listed call site of the protocol change) had to change to compile: its decision handler now validates the new shape and calls decide once with the docPath of the document it read, keeping its existing inline notices; the host tests pinned on approve()/comment() were rewritten to that. Known gap until task 9 rebuilds the shell: the current shell's two buttons still post the earlier accept/note shape, which the host now drops, so the pane's buttons do nothing between this task and task 9; the shell text and its pinned baseline are untouched here. docs-content's new fields, the result message, the chat message and the companion handling are task 8. Plugin test files are excluded from the plugin's tsc; I compiled the two changed test files once with a temporary tsconfig and they typecheck. Plugin suite without forced exit: 1217 tests, 1207 pass, 8 skipped, 2 fail (src/config/__tests__/manifest-catalog.test.ts, failing before this Story).",
